  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">What works: Best Practices in MHPSS for Preventing and Responding to SEC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This research project aims to generate evidence on best practices in mental health and psychosocial support interventions for the prevention and response to SEC. By reviewing a range of existing interventions, particularly those rooted in peer support, family, and community approaches, the study will identify and explore 3-4 promising models in depth. The findings will inform future TDH NL programming by providing practical guidance on effective, scalable, and contextually relevant MHPSS-SEC interventions</narrative>
  </description>
